# Confirmed facts and their sources

This is a fictional derivative. `confirmations.md` distinguishes its new
decisions from the historical source. The old CV is preserved in
`material/cv.md` as conflicting source material, not publication-ready copy.

| Fact | Source and limits |
|---|---|
| Ada Mensah works with embedded firmware for physical devices | Original `material/cv.md`; confirmed audience and contribution in the saved fictional replies. No current employer/title/date claim is needed. |
| Mosslink is an environmental sensor | Original `material/cv.md`. It is an invented project, not a real product or employer disclosure. |
| Ada wrote firmware, scheduled power states and built the bring-up fixture | Historical fictional confirmation overrides "Owned the low-power sensor design" in the original CV. |
| A colleague designed the PCB and analogue front end | Historical fictional confirmation. Ada must not be credited with this circuitry. |
| Two years is a projection from bench current readings and an assumed reporting cycle | Historical fictional confirmation plus `material/lab-notes.md`. No exact reporting interval, current value, capacity, climate condition or model ownership is supplied. |
| The longest run was 72 hours | Historical fictional confirmation plus `material/lab-notes.md`. It does not establish projected endurance, field endurance or weather testing. |
| Forty engineering samples assembled; six tested on the bench; none sent to customers | Historical fictional confirmation overrides "forty-unit pilot". No field pilot, product launch or forty-unit verification. |
| One preliminary emissions check passed; full qualification unfinished | Historical fictional confirmation overrides "Qualification: emissions pass". No certification claim. |
| State tables, timing diagrams and current traces are daily working documents | Historical fictional confirmation plus lab notes. No actual trace is supplied or licensed for display. |
| Bring-up means checking a new board's basic operation | Historical fictional confirmation. |
| The audience is a firmware hiring manager; email and downloadable CV are enough | Historical fictional confirmation. |
| No old site and no testimonials | Historical fictional confirmation. |
| Public email, schematic assets, HTML CV and static-mode choices are confirmed for this derivative | New, explicitly fictional `confirmations.md`. |

## Resolved source disagreements

Use the corrected contribution, projection, sample and preliminary-status
wording above. The original CV remains unchanged in `material/` for source
provenance. The public corrected CV contains only the narrower claims.

## Omitted because evidence is absent

The lab notes mention a failed transmission leaving the radio awake. They
do not establish who diagnosed or fixed it, a measured outcome, or a public
incident account. Do not turn it into a success story. No real trace,
circuit diagram, employer firmware, qualification report, photograph or
field deployment is supplied. The new explanatory SVGs are not substitutes
for those records and must retain their visible explanatory labels.

No influence story, testimonial, additional project, career chronology or
confirmed current employer title/date is supplied. The scope avoids them.

## Provenance of the confirmations

The historical source is the fictional `embedded` person and the saved
`codex-opening-1/embedded/with-2` conversation. The coordinator retains the
original files and hashes outside this actor workspace. All new scope
decisions are enumerated in `confirmations.md`; none is attributed to the
real repository author. Original facts do not become real-world claims by
appearing in this build fixture.
